(NATIVECAM ROTARY CHECK: times the rotary A axis. Nothing but A moves: X, Y and Z stay where they)
(are.)
(Take any stock out of the chuck. Raise the bit well clear of the chuck and tailstock before)
(starting.)
(There's no tool change: leave any bit in, with Z zeroed on the work as usual. The first stop is)
(there to confirm it.)
(Zero A where it is now {any angle will do}. Keep the overrides at 100%.)
(At each stop the message names the next turn. Press Cycle Start and time it from the first move)
(until the machine stops. The first turn, in inverse time {G93 F10}, should take 6 s.)
(NativeCAM rotary check)
(Post: Avid CNC Mach4 - NativeCAM calibration)
